Fix AOT compatibility warnings in these files under /tmp/sv-17bdfbddaf634aeeb47524c30f4ffda7/before/.

## 1. Common/Custom/Models/ManagedServiceIdentity.Serialization.cs

This file has 4 JsonSerializer calls that need fixing. The types used have custom `JsonConverter`s but also have `IJsonModel<T>` implementations and static Deserialize methods.

### Line 31: `JsonSerializer.Serialize(writer, ManagedServiceIdentityType, jOptions)`
The `ManagedServiceIdentityType` has a `JsonConverter` that writes `writer.WritePropertyName("type"); writer.WriteStringValue(model.ToString())`. Replace with inline logic:
```csharp
// Before:
JsonSerializer.Serialize(writer, ManagedServiceIdentityType, jOptions);
// After:
writer.WritePropertyName("type"u8);
writer.WriteStringValue(ManagedServiceIdentityType.ToString());
```

### Line 49: `JsonSerializer.Serialize(writer, item.Value, jOptions)`
`item.Value` is `UserAssignedIdentity` which implements `IJsonModel<UserAssignedIdentity>`. Replace with:
```csharp
// Before:
JsonSerializer.Serialize(writer, item.Value, jOptions);
// After:
writer.WriteObjectValue(item.Value, ModelSerializationExtensions.WireOptions);
```

### Line 206: `type = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<ManagedServiceIdentityType>($"{{{property}}}");`
The converter's `Read` method parses JSON like `{"type":"SystemAssigned"}` and returns `new ManagedServiceIdentityType(property.Value.GetString())`. Replace with inline:
```csharp
// Before:
type = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<ManagedServiceIdentityType>($"{{{property}}}");
// After:
type = new ManagedServiceIdentityType(property.Value.GetString());
```

### Line 218: `dictionary.Add(new ResourceIdentifier(property0.Name), JsonSerializer.Deserialize<UserAssignedIdentity>(property0.Value.GetRawText()));`
Replace with:
```csharp
// Before:
dictionary.Add(new ResourceIdentifier(property0.Name), JsonSerializer.Deserialize<UserAssignedIdentity>(property0.Value.GetRawText()));
// After:
dictionary.Add(new ResourceIdentifier(property0.Name), UserAssignedIdentity.DeserializeUserAssignedIdentity(property0.Value));
```

## 2. ArmEnvironment.cs

### Line 80: `public override string ToString() => JsonSerializer.Serialize(this);`
`ArmEnvironment` is a struct with `Endpoint` (Uri) and `Audience` (string) properties. Replace with manual JSON construction:
```csharp
// Before:
public override string ToString() => JsonSerializer.Serialize(this);
// After:
public override string ToString() => $"{{\"Endpoint\":\"{Endpoint}\",\"Audience\":\"{Audience}\"}}";
```

## 3. ArmClientOptions.cs

### Line 52: `var allProfile = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span);`
This needs a source-generated `JsonSerializerContext`. Create a new file at `/tmp/sv-17bdfbddaf634aeeb47524c30f4ffda7/before/ArmSerializerContext.cs` with:
```csharp
